  <!-- ETP-5222 (Item 4, 2026-09-09): standard Invoice Price Variance account for all clients is GL
       99904000 ("Diferencias entre el coste del producto y el precio de la fra[ctura]"). This
       column shipped NULL in the bundled dataset (the gap this ticket closes) even though every
       sibling *_ACCT column here is populated.

       ID SOURCING (do not source this kind of value from a live DB query — verified from the
       BUNDLE FILES themselves, since this whole directory is imported per new tenant with ID
       TRANSLATION, see below): the id below is C_VALIDCOMBINATION.xml's own row for account
       99904000 (C_VALIDCOMBINATION_ID=29616DEC549948E7A65ABC28BCC18742, ACCOUNT_ID resolves to
       C_ELEMENTVALUE_ID=E8537B8CCACC48BCBD2B3FED4D009242, VALUE=99904000, ELEMENTLEVEL=S, no
       dimension columns present i.e. a natural/dimensionless combination) — a row DEFINED WITHIN
       THIS SAME referencedata/sampledata/GOClient/ bundle, exactly the same pattern P_EXPENSE_ACCT
       above already follows (its own id D3169915F5E34F51B67E6F5FA0855D86 is likewise a
       C_VALIDCOMBINATION.xml row in this bundle, not a live-DB artifact). The C_ELEMENTVALUE row is
       reached through C_ACCTSCHEMA_ELEMENT/elementtype='AC' (C_ELEMENT_ID=BB9B64C5B6534A40A36F7C0F
       45C2CC0B) to avoid the orphan "GOOrg Account Tree" element that ALSO carries a second,
       unwired C_ELEMENTVALUE row for 99904000 in this same bundle.

       WHY REFERENCING ANOTHER FILE IN THIS BUNDLE BY ITS LITERAL ID IS SAFE FOR A NEW TENANT: this
       whole directory is imported as ONE batch by OnboardingDatasetImportService ->
       DataImportService#importDataFromXML (core's own reference-data importer). Every NEW tenant
       gets a freshly auto-generated PK per inserted row (org.openbravo.service.db.
       DataImportService#saveUpdateConvertedObjects -> insertObjectGraph, standard DAL insert) — the
       literal ids in this XML are NEVER reused verbatim for a new tenant. What ties this file's
       reference to the correct freshly-generated row is core's id-translation mechanism
       (EntityResolver#getId / AD_REF_DATA_LOADED = ReferenceDataStore, generic=<this literal id> ->
       specific=<the new tenant's freshly generated id for the SAME source row>, scoped per client)
       — the exact mechanism P_EXPENSE_ACCT above already relies on. Confirmed empirically too: two
       independently-onboarded local tenants (GOClient itself and "SantoEmpresa") hold DIFFERENT
       c_elementvalue_id/c_validcombination_id pairs for the very same account 99904000, proving
       each tenant's chart is its own freshly-generated clone, not a shared/literal copy of
       GOClient's ids. This is the dataset-import-time baseline (Layer 0): the Java runtime patch
       (OnboardingAccountingWiringService#backfillInvoicePriceVarianceDefault) remains as the
       self-healing backstop for any provisioning path that does not read this file, and correctly
       no-ops once this column is already set by the import. -->
